    "enrich_notes": "WQv uses P=1 inch (Reduced Runoff and Volume Based methods). WQv draw-down 12–48 hr (SW11.07). SHWT setback varies: 2 ft (many BMPs), 3 ft (water quality swale), 4 ft (permeable pavement, retention basin eligibility). Bioretention also requires ≥18 in soil/media infiltration path before underdrain for WQ credit; filter media infiltration ≥0.5 in/hr; dewatering 24–72 hr. Swale WQv ponding cap 12 in for 1 in WQv; soil infiltration >1 in/hr without underdrain. Proprietary units sized on 0.3 in rainfall SCS rate (SW11.08). Forebay length:width ≥3:1.",
